        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "332ec40c-1cb3-5559-9af5-af28c9210379",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Charles Runnington, John Runnington\n- Places: Hertfordshire, Hertford, southern England, Bedfordshire, Cambridgeshire, Essex, Buckinghamshire, Greater London\n- Roles: serjeant-at-law, mayor of Hertford\n- Organizations: Inner Temple\n\nFacts:\n- Charles Runnington was born in Hertfordshire on 29 August 1751.\n- John Runnington was probably Charles Runnington’s father and was mayor of Hertford in 1754.\n- Charles Runnington was educated under private tutors and spent some years in special pleading.\n- Charles Runnington was called to the bar at the Inner Temple in Hilary term 1778.\n- Charles Runnington lived from 1751 to 1821 and was a serjeant-at-law.\n- Hertfordshire is a county in southern England.\n- Hertfordshire is often abbreviated Herts.\n- Hertfordshire borders Bedfordshire to the north, Cambridgeshire to the north-east, Essex to the east, Buckinghamshire to the west, and Greater London to the south.",
